UPDATE "base_parameters" SET "updated_at" = '2026-09-17 22:13', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-17-engine-proxy-inference', "direction_rationale" = 'A gentler ramp is more accessible, and the admitted evidence states it rather than the engine assuming it. REF-00996 (Handboek Toegankelijkheid) gives both the criterion and its mechanism: hoe groter het hoogteverschil, hoe zachter de helling moet zijn, omdat men gedurende een langere tijd een inspanning moet leveren — the greater the rise, the gentler the ramp must be, because the effort must be sustained longer — with the physical feasibility of the independently self-propelling wheelchair user as the starting point. REF-00987 (ADA) says it in its own advisory to 405.2: provide ramps with the least possible running slope. REF-00994 (IPC) frames 1:20 as best practice and 1:14 as a concession for ancillary facilities only, which is the same direction stated as a preference ordering. The T1 dose-response rows measure it: articular discomfort and pushrim force both rise with gradient across the tested range. Four sources, three strata, one direction, none contradicted — derived, not adjudicated. NOT contested: no admitted source identifies a population for whom a steeper ramp is better. Recorded because compose_value cannot select most-accommodatingly without it and was returning a NULL interval with that exact complaint.', "accessibility_direction" = 'lower_is_better' WHERE "parameter_id" = 3;

